  <name>Tuxsitter</name>
  <summary>Simple parental controls for Linux desktops</summary>
  <summary xml:lang="de">Einfache Kindersicherung für Linux-Desktops</summary>
  <summary xml:lang="fr">Contrôle parental simple pour les bureaux Linux</summary>
  <summary xml:lang="es">Control parental sencillo para escritorios Linux</summary>
  <developer id="io.github.chpusch">
    <name>chpusch</name>
  </developer>
  <description>
    <p>
      Tuxsitter is a small, friendly babysitter for the family computer. Parents get one simple
      window; the child sees how much time is left in the panel.
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>Daily screen time with separate limits for school days and weekends, plus a holiday mode</li>
      <li>Allowed hours, fair warnings and a countdown before logout</li>
      <li>Extra time with a parent PIN, right on the child's computer</li>
      <li>Internet filter for the child's account only, with a family DNS provider of your choice,
        SafeSearch and YouTube Restricted Mode</li>
      <li>History of the last 14 days</li>
      <li>No accounts, no cloud, no telemetry</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Made for Linux Mint (Cinnamon); works on other Ubuntu/Debian based desktops.</p>
  </description>
